# Testing

| Layer | How | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Domain | pure unit tests over event sequences | `crates/domain/src/room.rs` |
| Application | service tests with in-file fakes for every port | bottom of `crates/application/src/service.rs` |
| Adapters | real temp dirs, private tmux socket, temp git repos, the real process table (`awr-procs`), Node for the KWin script | each file in `crates/infrastructure/src` |
| Front | Vitest next to the code; fixtures in `src/test/fixtures.ts`; the store tested against the demo gateway | `src/**/*.test.ts` |
| UI look | screenshots of the demo UI | `npm run shot -- <dir>` |
| End to end | real `claude`/`codex` + real bridge + real socket, isolated; shared harness in `tests/e2e/mod.rs` | `claude_e2e.rs`, `codex_e2e.rs` in `crates/infrastructure/tests` (ignored) |
| Bridge end to end | contract-shaped Cursor/Antigravity payloads through the real bridge, socket and service | `bridge_e2e.rs` (ignored, needs the built bridge, costs nothing) |
| Live desktop | real KWin, real transcript | `kwin_live`, `transcript_live` (ignored) |

## Commands

- `scripts/check.sh` — scoped to what changed vs HEAD; one line per step, details only on failure
  (clippy `-D warnings`, cargo tests, tsc, vitest; docs check when docs changed).
- `scripts/check.sh all|rust|front|docs`.
- `scripts/cross_check.sh [windows|macos]` — clippy for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` and
  `aarch64-apple-darwin` from Linux, with zig as the C cross compiler (`pip install ziglang`) and
  stand-ins for Objective-C sources and Windows resources. Type-checks every `cfg` branch; links and
  runs nothing. Run it after touching anything `#[cfg]`-gated or OS-specific.
- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): clippy + tests + front on Linux, macOS and Windows runners; the
  `bundle` job (manual or `v*` tag) builds every installer. The only place macOS/Windows tests run.
- Unit tests that need Unix (`/bin/sh`, sockets) are `#[cfg(unix)]`; keep new ones portable or gate them.
- Ignored tests: run only when asked or when touching that integration; tell the user (they cost a
  Claude call or touch the desktop).

## Trigger table

| If you… | Read |
|---|---|
| run or write a real-Claude e2e, or drive a TUI in a PTY | `testing-e2e.md` |
| need screenshots of a state the demo doesn't have | extend `src/infrastructure/demoGateway.ts`, then `npm run shot` |
